<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ymer Prizreni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1820">1820</a>–<a href="/years/1887">1887</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ymer Prizreni was an Albanian Ottoman official and leader of the League of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prizren">Prizren</a>, formed in 1878 to resist the transfer of Albanian-inhabited lands to Montenegro, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. He headed the league's provisional government in 1881, before the Ottoman army suppressed the movement, and he died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulcinj">Ulcinj</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ymer-prizreni.jpg" alt="Ymer Prizreni" width="225" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of Albania · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ymer_Prizreni_2008_stamp_of_Albania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
